/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Artificial intelligence \(AI\) is emerging rapidly across industries, including K-12 education. The Delaware Council on Educational Technology presents this guidance to support educators and education leaders in the appropriate, equitable, and inclusive use of AI in classrooms across the State of Delaware.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Included in this Guidance Document)
/E (Included in this Guidance Document)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
439 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1109 0 R
/ActualText (Understanding AI)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
440 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1110 0 R
/ActualText (Delve into artificial intelligence, clarify its definition, weigh the advantages and disadvantages of its use in education, and dispel common myths surrounding its capabilities and limitations. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1111 0 R
/ActualText (Implementing Generative AI in Delaware Districts and Charters)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
442 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1112 0 R
/ActualText (The comprehensive recommendations address crucial policy areas such as protecting student data, ensuring ethical, equitable, and effective Generative AI use, promoting equity, and enhancing learning through content and curricula that leverage Generative AI technologies. Best practices are provided with implementation strategies, suggestions for managing platforms, and tools for evaluating Generative AI products.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1113 0 R
/ActualText (Integrating Generative AI into the Classroom)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
444 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1114 0 R
/ActualText (This section provides optimal practices for integrating Generative AI within the classroom. It emphasizes applications and strategies to enhance educational experiences, demonstrating how tools and applications support teaching and learning processes. The SAMR model includes illustrations to show how applications may align to each level. Also included are strategies for addressing academic dishonesty and ensuring that Generative AI tools are used responsibly in educational settings.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1115 0 R
/ActualText (Professional Learning)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1116 0 R
/ActualText (The final section suggests a framework for professional learning, listing essential topics and subject areas on which school districts and charter schools may choose to focus. Scalable training and delivery methods are recommended to guarantee that all educators and students across Delaware have equal opportunities to benefit from Generative AI technologies. This approach aims to equip teachers with the knowledge and skills necessary to integrate Generative AI into their teaching practices effectively, thereby enhancing the educational experience for students.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
